cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SciField — 78-journal literature cartography of surgery (V2 cartography release)"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Samer
    name-particle: G.
    family-names: Salman
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-9897-4071"
    affiliation: "Baylor College of Medicine"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-06-22"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/samersalman/scifield"
url: "https://github.com/samersalman/scifield"
abstract: >
  SciField maps the health and movement of a scientific field. This V2
  cartography release (v0.2.0) maps the surgical literature across a 78-journal
  panel on a 1.49M-paper corpus: a topic landscape (149 leaf topics over a
  leaf->mid->top hierarchy), journal-to-journal cascade lead-lag diffusion,
  source / bridge / terminal journal roles, and novelty origins by institution
  sector and country (V2-S09); a descriptive per-topic trajectory layer (V2-S10)
  projecting share and volume +5 years to 2030 with 80% bands (descriptive
  extrapolation, not a forecast); and an interactive static 5-tab map. The
  release deposits the derived cartography tables (~1.7 MB) with provenance
  sidecars; the raw corpus is reproducible from the pipeline, not redistributed.
  See docs/cartography/data-dictionary.md for the data dictionary and caveats.
keywords:
